WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:07.060
The Drac Pack is back with more zing and bleh-bleh-bleh
in the animated movie Hotel Transylvania 3!

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:11.389
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and today I'm revealing 10 fiendishly freaky

00:00:11.389 --> 00:00:15.309
and fun facts you need to know about the latest
monster-filled sequel!

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:18.800
Just before we start make sure you subscribe
and hit the bell to stay up-to-date with all

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:20.000
my new videos.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.419
Among the new characters in Hotel T3 is Chupacabra
who's named after a mythical monster which

00:00:25.419 --> 00:00:27.759
has its origins in Latin America.

00:00:27.759 --> 00:00:32.150
In the movie, Chupacabra appears at the ship's
bar where he has a drink made up of a goat

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.060
stuffed into a martini glass.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:38.960
This is a freakily funny moment because in
Spanish Chupacabra literally means "goat-sucker",

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.210
a name the creature got because of stories
about it attacking goats and drinking their

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.740
blood like a vampire.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:48.720
Curiously, the filmmakers were originally
going to use a different bogeyman-type character

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.550
called "El Coco", however, it tested badly
in an early screening so it was cut and Chupacabra

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:55.070
took its place.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.300
The Drac Pack set off on their vacation on
a plane that caters for monsters called Gremlin

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.300
Air.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.080
The name of the airline and the fact it's
run by ill-behaved beasts is a cool shout-out

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.609
to the origin of the word "gremlin".

00:01:05.609 --> 00:01:11.039
The word was originally used by pilots in
the Royal Air Force who blamed faults in their

00:01:11.039 --> 00:01:15.869
planes on impish little creatures that they
called gremlins who they said sabotaged their

00:01:15.869 --> 00:01:16.869
aircraft.

00:01:16.869 --> 00:01:21.140
The filmmakers really took this idea to heart
so the Gremlin Air scenes feature an ancient

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:25.289
bomber plane which has been rebuilt and patched
back together so many times that you can see

00:01:25.289 --> 00:01:29.780
duct tape everywhere, different colour seats
made from different materials, plywood on

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:32.619
the floor, and loose wires all over the place.

00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:36.889
And the badly behaved gremlins working on
the flight are green, like many of the monstrous

00:01:36.889 --> 00:01:41.049
creatures in the classic 1980s horror comedy
Gremlins.

00:01:41.049 --> 00:01:45.259
If you think Dennis's dog Tinkles is big,
just wait till you see the Kraken that protects

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:49.469
the lost city of Atlantis, a sort of monster
version of Las Vegas!

00:01:49.469 --> 00:01:54.469
Singer Joe Jonas voices the Kraken which is
such an absolutely enormous character that

00:01:54.469 --> 00:01:58.780
it almost broke the simulation software when
the animators made it move and dance through

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.780
the water.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.590
The reason for that is because the very cartoony
style of the Hotel T movies doesn't lend itself

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.780
to the physics of real water that the software
tries to emulate.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:12.620
To solve the problem of how to animate the
huge impact the Kraken has on the water, the

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:18.390
visual effects team looked at footage of large-scale
water events to see how the water behaves,

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:22.660
for example, crashing waves, boats being launched,
and giant ice structures falling into the

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:23.660
ocean.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:27.370
They discovered that, during those events,
there's a lot of water vapour generated and

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:31.680
the water tends to get very frothy and white,
so, they emulated that vapour layer in the

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:36.319
film and they also slowed down the speed at
which the Kraken's giant tentacles hit the

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:40.040
water so the splashes weren't so explosive.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:44.459
Even freakier than a luxury cruise for monsters
is the fact that the ship's crew is actually

00:02:44.459 --> 00:02:48.720
made up of Fish-Men, which are kind of like
reverse Mermen, with a fishy top-half and

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.349
a human bottom half!

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:54.819
You'll see these scaly creatures with human-looking
feet and fins for hands working in a variety

00:02:54.819 --> 00:03:01.879
of areas on board including as barmen, musicians,
taking photos of guests, and even giving manicures

00:03:01.879 --> 00:03:02.879
and massages!

00:03:02.879 --> 00:03:05.970
And, if you look carefully, you'll notice
the Fish-Men often only move a little, for

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:11.110
example, just their mouths or eyes, and when
they do move, they don't bend forward.

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:15.230
That's because fish can only actually bend
sideways, so the director made sure the animators

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:16.489
reflected that in the movie!

00:03:16.489 --> 00:03:19.409
"Everybody, just please watch the hair.

00:03:19.409 --> 00:03:22.140
Watch the hair!"

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.219
As you can tell, Eunice really isn't keen
on getting her hair wet, which seems funny

00:03:26.219 --> 00:03:30.870
when you find out that the animators actually
based Eunice's hairstyle on a Brillo pad,

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:34.219
a type of scouring pad used for cleaning dishes!

00:03:34.219 --> 00:03:38.480
Speaking of hair, when the character designers
first created Mavis and Johnny's son, Dennis,

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:41.849
they drew him with a huge mane of red hair,
like his father.

00:03:41.849 --> 00:03:46.260
But when they animated that design on a computer,
they found Dennis' hair looked too big for

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.260
his head to hold!

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:52.180
In fact, Dennis' hair took up so much room
that Mavis and Johnny would have needed arms

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.360
twice the length in order to pick him up.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.390
So, the designers gave him a haircut!

00:03:56.390 --> 00:04:01.870
Originally, Dennis' giant dog Tinkles was
only going to appear very briefly in Hotel

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.050
Transylvania 3.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:07.349
However, after fans enjoyed his character
so much when they met him for the first time

00:04:07.349 --> 00:04:11.670
in the short film, Puppy!, the filmmakers
decided to make Tinkles a much bigger part

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:13.269
of the new sequel.

00:04:13.269 --> 00:04:17.421
To work out how to animate the scene where
Drac gets champagne thrown at his face, one

00:04:17.421 --> 00:04:22.049
of the animators had a champagne bottle popped
open near his face a dozen times!

00:04:22.049 --> 00:04:26.520
Obviously it hurt, so definitely do not try
anything like that at home!

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:31.740
One of the biggest challenges of animating
Drac is actually his cape, so because he wears

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:36.289
shorts and an Hawaiian shirt while on vacation
in Hotel T3 that made life quite a bit easier

00:04:36.289 --> 00:04:38.110
for the animators this time!

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:41.190
And talking of Drac's vacation clothes, did
you notice his shoes?

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:46.650
Well, they're an easter egg to the 1980s comedy
movie National Lampoon's Vacation which starred

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:49.630
Chevy Chase and was a big inspiration for
Hotel T3.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:54.340
Both movies feature a family going on vacation
together and the various mishaps they have

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:55.340
along the way.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:58.770
Now, who's your favourite character in the
Hotel Transylvania movies?

